package mcp

// The tools/list entries of the cost tools, as src/mcp.ts's JSON.stringify writes them (generated by testdata/genlistings.mjs; mcp_test.go compares).
var costListings = map[string]string{
	"usage_info":    "{\"name\":\"usage_info\",\"group\":\"cost\",\"description\":\"Spend and tokens by day, model, and agent, and subscription windows (such as Claude 5-hour and weekly limits), with estimated shares of each window by agent and tree, the usual percent per hour by hour of day and weekday, and when it reaches 100% (at the rate of the last 30 minutes, and following the usual pattern), the trees' allocations with their current use, plus the user's cost instructions. Compact by default (the windows with their projections, the top 5 trees, agents and models, the allocations, the machines); pass detail (true) for every agent, tree, model and cost unit with the hourly history, about 1 MB. Pass tree (an agent name or id) for that tree's estimated share and hourly history of each window, its allocations, and what a finished issue with its root's harness and model typically used. Use it to plan cost-aware work, for example picking a cheaper preset. It also includes machines: each computer's one-minute CPU, RAM, and swap averages, load, and its agents by state (null from a peer on an older release), to schedule work by load.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"days\":{\"type\":\"number\"},\"tree\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"An agent name or id: show its tree's estimated share of each window.\"},\"detail\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"The whole route answer, about 1 MB, not the compact one. False by default.\"}}}}",
	"cost_allocate": "{\"name\":\"cost_allocate\",\"group\":\"cost\",\"description\":\"Set or clear an allocation on a tree: how much of an account's subscription window (kind 'window' with a percent), or how many paid dollars per period (kind 'usd' with an amount and a period of day, week, or month), the tree may use. The user sets any allocation, the chief of staff any, every other agent only trees inside its own tree. Allocations are not enforced: at 80% and 100% of an allocation the tree's manager and its root get a cost notice. Setting one that pushes children past their parent tree's allocation warns but is not refused. Pass clear: true (with id, or tree/account/kind/scope) to remove one.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"tree\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The tree's root agent, by id or name.\"},\"account\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The cost account, such as claude or openrouter.\"},\"kind\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"window\",\"usd\"]},\"window\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"For kind 'window': the window name, such as five_hour.\"},\"percent\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"For kind 'window': the allocated percentage of the window.\"},\"amount\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"For kind 'usd': the allocated dollars.\"},\"period\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"day\",\"week\",\"month\"],\"description\":\"For kind 'usd': the period.\"},\"note\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Optional note, carried in the notices.\"},\"clear\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Remove the matching allocation instead of setting one.\"},\"id\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"With clear: the allocation id.\"}}}}",
	"cost_ack":      "{\"name\":\"cost_ack\",\"group\":\"cost\",\"description\":\"Record that you handled a cost notice, keyed by the event id in the notice. It stops the fallback timer for that event (the timer itself comes later). A manager calls this after it acts on a notice about its tree.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"event\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The event id from the cost notice, for example cn-1a2b3c4d.\"}},\"required\":[\"event\"]}}",
	"cost_switch":   "{\"name\":\"cost_switch\",\"group\":\"cost\",\"description\":\"Move an agent's work to another preset, for example when its account is exhausted. The agent gets time to finish its step and update HANDOVER.md (cost.softStopMinutes, default 10), then stam stops its harness (keeping its session) and holds it as taken over. A successor NAME-t2 starts on the preset in the same workspace, with the same parents, the agent's children, open threads and unread mail, and mail to the old name goes to it. Refused when the preset's account is blocked. A manager may switch agents in its own tree; the chief of staff and the human any. The predecessor's open cost notices are acknowledged. A working agent switches in the background and you hear the outcome.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"agent\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The agent whose work moves: an id or name.\"},\"preset\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The preset to move it to; registry_info lists them.\"},\"soft_stop_minutes\":{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Minutes the agent gets to finish its step before stam interrupts it. Defaults to cost.softStopMinutes.\"}},\"required\":[\"agent\",\"preset\"]}}",
	"cost_pause":    "{\"name\":\"cost_pause\",\"group\":\"cost\",\"description\":\"Pause a tree for cost until one of its subscription windows resets, or until a set time; stam lifts the pause by itself. Pass until=\\\"reset\\\" (with an account and window; the default window is the one closest to 100% on the tree's account) or an ISO 8601 time. Pass clear:true to lift an earlier cost pause early. The tree is the agent you name and everything below it, and agents spawned into it while it is paused are held too. A manager may pause its own tree; the chief of staff and the human may pause any. Calling this also acknowledges the tree's open cost notices.\",\"inputSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"self\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Your stam agent id. Needed only when your system prompt asks for it.\"},\"tree\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The tree root: an agent id or name.\"},\"until\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"\\\"reset\\\", or an ISO 8601 time such as 2026-10-12T09:00:00Z.\"},\"account\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"For until=reset: the cost account. Defaults to the tree's account.\"},\"window\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"For until=reset: the window, for example five_hour. Defaults to the window closest to 100%.\"},\"clear\":{\"type\":\"boolean\",\"description\":\"Remove the tree's cost pause early, instead of setting one.\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Why, for the resume notice and the record.\"}},\"required\":[\"tree\"]}}",
}
